## ShowMeTheKey

KDE KeyCast includes a modified version of the ShowMeTheKey command-line backend.

The bundled backend is located in:

    vendor/showmethekey-cli/

The original ShowMeTheKey license is preserved in:

    vendor/showmethekey-cli/LICENSE

License: Apache License 2.0.

The KDE KeyCast version contains modifications to add physical mouse wheel event
detection.

## AppImage build tools

The repository includes prebuilt AppImage build tools used to create the KDE KeyCast
AppImage:

- linuxdeploy — MIT License
- linuxdeploy-plugin-qt — MIT License
- appimagetool — MIT License

These tools are build-time dependencies only. They are not runtime dependencies of
KDE KeyCast and are not included as components of the generated KDE KeyCast AppImage.

The official projects are:

- linuxdeploy: https://github.com/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy
- linuxdeploy-plugin-qt: https://github.com/linuxdeploy/linuxdeploy-plugin-qt
- appimagetool: https://github.com/AppImage/appimagetool

## AppImage runtime components

The generated KDE KeyCast AppImage contains third-party runtime libraries and
components, including Qt, Wayland, xkbcommon, libinput, libevdev and other
dependencies.

These components retain their respective licenses and copyright notices.

The AppImage build process preserves the copyright and license information provided
by the corresponding packages under:

    usr/share/doc/

within the AppImage.

The complete licensing information for each bundled component should be consulted
there when redistributing or modifying the AppImage.

## KDE and other external dependencies

KDE KeyCast also uses external software and libraries provided by the target Linux
distribution, including Qt, KDE Frameworks, Wayland, xkbcommon, libinput, libevdev,
libudev and related system components.

These dependencies are not part of the KDE KeyCast source code and remain subject
to their respective licenses.

